lesson: 92
title: Buying several things at one price
stars: 0
explain: When every thing costs the same, the total cost is the price of one times the number of things.
explain: 6 pencils at 15 cents each cost 6 × 15 = 90 cents.
vars: a=name i=item n=2..9 p=2..25
answer: n * p
exercise: {a} buys {n} {i}s. Each {i} costs {p} cents. How many cents does {a.he} pay?
exercise: One {i} costs {p} cents. How much do {n} {i}s cost, in cents?
exercise: {a} wants {n} {i}s at {p} cents each. What is the total cost in cents?
exercise: A shop sells one {i} for {p} dollars. {a} buys {n} of them. How many dollars does {a.he} spend?
exercise: {n} {i}s cost {p} dollars each. How many dollars do they cost together?
exercise: {a} gets {n} {i}s for {a.his} class. Every {i} is {p} cents. How many cents does {a.he} spend?
test: What is the price of {n} {i}s if just one {i} is sold for {p} cents?
test: The price tag says {p} dollars for one {i}. {a} takes {n}. How many dollars must {a.he} pay at the till?
test: {a} pays for {n} {i}s, and the shopkeeper charges {p} cents for each one. How many cents is the bill?
test: Each {i} at the fair costs {p} cents. If {a} buys {n} {i}s, how much money in cents does {a.he} hand over?
exercise: {a} buys {n} {i}s for {p} cents apiece. How many cents does {a.he} spend in all?
exercise: How many cents do {n} {i}s cost if each one is {p} cents?
exercise: {n} {i}s at {p} cents per {i}. How many cents altogether?
exercise: A store in Ohio sells {i}s for {p} dollars each. {a} buys {n}. How many dollars does {a.he} pay in total?
exercise: {a} picks up {n.words} {i}s, and every {i} costs {p} cents. What does {a.he} pay, in cents?
exercise: The price of one {i} is {p} cents. What do {n} {i}s cost combined, in cents?
exercise: At a market in Leeds, {a} buys {n} {i}s. Each costs {p} pounds. How many pounds does {a.he} spend?
exercise: {a} orders {n} {i}s at {p} dollars per {i}. How many dollars is the total?
test: How much does {a} spend in cents for {n} {i}s if the shop asks {p} cents for every single one?
test: A shop in Melbourne charges {p} dollars for one {i}. {a} buys {n.words} of them. How many dollars is that?
test: For a school trip, {a} gets {n} {i}s; each one is priced at {p} cents. What is the cost in cents?
test: Into the basket go {n} {i}s, and the label on each says {p} cents. How many cents must {a} pay?
test: {a} pays the same {p} cents for each of {n} {i}s at a corner shop in Belfast. How many cents does {a.he} pay altogether?
test: The bill: {n} {i}s, {p} cents a piece. How many cents is the bill?
exercise: {n} {i}s at {p} cents each, how much in cents
exercise: {a} grabbed {n+1} {i}s — nah, {n}, put one back. {p}c each. cents total?
exercise: them {i}s is {p} cents each, {a} wants {n}, how many cents {a.he} gotta pay
exercise: {a} says {n} {i}s at {p} cents is {n*p+p} cents. nah whats the real cost in cents
test: {p} cents a {i}, i need {n} of em. cents?
test: how many cents for {n} {i}s if one's {p} cents — oh and the shop opens at 9 lol
test: {a} had {n+3} {i}s in the basket, no sorry, {n}, each {p} cents. what it cost in cents
exam: It is given that one {i} is priced at {p} cents. Determine the total expenditure, in cents, incurred in the purchase of {n} such {i}s.
exam: {a} purchases {n.words} {i}s at a unit price of {p} cents. Compute the aggregate sum payable, expressed in cents.
exam: Whereas each {i} is offered for sale at {p} cents, ascertain the cost in cents of {n} {i}s acquired by {a}.
exam: State, in cents, the total amount disbursed by {a} in respect of {n} {i}s, the price of each being {p} cents.
exercise: The shop calls it a "price adjustment": each {i} now costs {p} cents. {a} buys {n} {i}s. How many cents does {a.he} pay?
exercise: {a}'s family has fallen on hard times, so {a.he} buys just {n} {i}s at {p} cents each. How many cents does {a.he} spend?
test: "value" pack my foot — {n} {i}s at {p} cents a pop. how much is that, quick, the queue's moaning
